=== Prompt ===
Who is Link from Zelda?

=== Response ===
Link is the main protagonist in the popular video game series "The Legend of Zelda," created by Nintendo. He is a brave and skilled young hero who is tasked with saving the kingdom of Hyrule from various evils.

Link is often reincarnated in each game, with different versions of him appearing in different games within the series. However, he is typically depicted as a brave warrior, skilled in sword fighting and archery. He is also known for his ability to wield the Master Sword, a powerful blade that is said to be able to vanquish evil.

Throughout the series, Link is often aided by the princess of Hyrule, Zelda, who is the holder of the Triforce of Wisdom. Together, they must battle against the main antagonist, Ganon (also known as Ganondorf), who seeks to conquer Hyrule and destroy its people.

Link's character has become an iconic figure in gaming culture, and he has been featured in numerous games, TV shows, and other media within the Zelda franchise.

